APIMC - 4704 - Add Gateway Filter to API Catalog with Single-Select Dropdown

Add a new Gateway filter to the API Catalog page alongside the existing Domain filter. The Gateway filter allows users to filter APIs by a single gateway selection using radio buttons. Gateway options are fetched dynamically from an API endpoint and displayed in alphabetical order.
h2. Requirements
h3. New Filter: Gateway (Single-Select)

Add a new filter chip labeled "Gateway" that:
 * Appears after the Domain filter in the filter bar
 * Allows selection of ONE gateway at a time (radio buttons)
 * Fetches gateway options dynamically from API
 * Displays options in alphabetical ascending order
 * Can be used TOGETHER with Domain filter (not mutually exclusive)
 * Follows the same visual design pattern as Domain filter

h3. Gateway Options (Sample Data)

The following gateway names should be displayed (alphabetically sorted):
 * Enterprise
 * Mobile
 * Spectrum Payment Services
 * Video
 * Shared
 * None
 * Other
 * Private

h3. Gateway Filter Behavior

*Filter Combinations:*
 * View All and Favorites are mutually exclusive with all other filters
 * Domain and Gateway CAN be selected together
 * Selecting View All or Favorites clears both Domain and Gateway
 * Domain and Gateway selections do NOT clear each other

*Filter States:*
 # *No Selection (Default)*

 * 
 ** Display: "Gateway"
 ** Style: Gray background, dark text
 ** Click to open dropdown

 # *Gateway Selected*

 * 
 ** Display: "Gateway: [GatewayName]"
 ** Format: [Label] : [Value]
 ** Style: Black background, white text
 ** Shows close button (×)
 ** Click chip to edit, click × to clear
 ** Can coexist with Domain selections (both chips can be black simultaneously)

h3. Gateway Dropdown

*Opening:*
 * Click Gateway chip/button
 * Dropdown appears below the chip
 * Shows all gateway options with radio buttons
 * Previously selected gateway is pre-checked

*Selection:*
 * User can select ONE gateway (radio button behavior)
 * Selecting a new gateway automatically deselects the previous one

*Closing:*
 * {*}Click "Apply"{*}: Applies selection, closes dropdown, updates chip
 * {*}Click Outside{*}: Auto-applies selection, closes dropdown
 * {*}Click "Clear"{*}: Unchecks radio button, keeps dropdown open
 * {*}Click × on chip{*}: Clears selection, closes dropdown, returns to View All

h3. API Integration

*Endpoint:*
{code:java}
GET https://apis-internal-corp.shared.uat-spectrum.net/pinxt-selfservice/v1/gateway {code}
*Data Handling:*
 * Extract {{gatewayName}} from each object in the response array
 * Sort gateway names alphabetically (A-Z) before displaying
 * Use {{gatewayName}} for display and filtering

